{
  "$schema": "../schema/fixture-cases.schema.json",
  "client": "claude-code",
  "cases_version": 3,
  "_readme": [
    "The specification, expressed as examples. No implementation existed when these were written,",
    "so they define what both must do rather than describing what one happens to do.",
    "",
    "Inputs are exact bytes and repair expectations are exact bytes, because the promise being",
    "proven is a MINIMAL SPAN EDIT: only the target span changes and every other byte survives.",
    "A field-level assertion would let TypeScript and Python reformat differently and both pass.",
    "",
    "Every credential-shaped value carries a `fixture` marker; the validator rejects any that",
    "does not, so no live key can enter the corpus."
  ],
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "healthy",
      "description": "A correct remote-HTTP entry. Nothing to report but the connection itself.",
      "raw_files": {
        ".mcp.json": "{\n  \"mcpServers\": {\n    \"superdocs\": {\n      \"type\": \"http\",\n      \"url\": \"https://api.superdocs.app/mcp\",\n      \"headers\": {\n        \"Authorization\": \"Bearer sk_fixture_healthy_00000000\"\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n"
      },
      "expect": {
        "scan": {
          "exit_code": 0,
          "findings": []
        },
        "fix": {
          "exit_code": 0,
          "findings": [],
          "files_unchanged": true,
          "backup_expected": false
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "no-entry",
      "description": "Client configured, but no SuperDocs server. Not using SuperDocs is not a failure.",
      "raw_files": {
        ".mcp.json": "{\n  \"mcpServers\": {\n    \"postgres\": {\n      \"command\": \"npx\",\n      \"args\": [\"-y\", \"pg-mcp\"]\n    }\n  }\n}\n"
      },
      "env": {
        "SUPERDOCS_API_KEY": null
      },
      "expect": {
        "scan": {
          "exit_code": 0,
          "findings": [
            {
              "id": "config.no-entry",
              "severity": "info",
              "auto_fixable": true
            }
          ]
        },
        "fix": {
          "exit_code": 1,
          "findings": [
            {
              "id": "config.key-absent",
              "severity": "error"
            }
          ],
          "files_unchanged": true,
          "backup_expected": false
        }
      },
      "_why": "--fix may add a missing entry, but never invents a credential. With no key resolvable it exits 1 naming the variable and writes nothing."
    },
    {
      "name": "scheme-insecure",
      "description": "http:// on the canonical host. Repairable: same host, wrong scheme.",
      "raw_files": {
        ".mcp.json": "{\n  \"mcpServers\": {\n    \"superdocs\": {\n      \"type\": \"http\",\n      \"url\": \"http://api.superdocs.app/mcp\",\n      \"headers\": {\n        \"Authorization\": \"Bearer sk_fixture_scheme_00000000\"\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n"
      },
      "expect": {
        "scan": {
          "exit_code": 1,
          "findings": [
            {
              "id": "config.scheme-insecure",
              "severity": "error",
              "auto_fixable": true
            }
          ]
        },
        "fix": {
          "exit_code": 0,
          "findings": [
            {
              "id": "config.scheme-insecure",
              "fixed": true
            }
          ],
          "backup_expected": true,
          "files": {
            ".mcp.json": "{\n  \"mcpServers\": {\n    \"superdocs\": {\n      \"type\": \"http\",\n      \"url\": \"https://api.superdocs.app/mcp\",\n      \"headers\": {\n        \"Authorization\": \"Bearer sk_fixture_scheme_00000000\"\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n"
          }
        }
      },
      "_why": "Exactly four bytes differ. Indentation, key order and the trailing newline are identical, which is what a span edit guarantees and a reserialise would not."
    },
