    {
      "name": "duplicate-key-shadows-a-value",
      "description": "The same key twice. JSON keeps the last silently, so a wrong value above a right one looks like a working config that does not work.",
      "raw_files": {
        ".mcp.json": "{\n  \"mcpServers\": {\n    \"superdocs\": {\n      \"type\": \"http\",\n      \"url\": \"http://api.superdocs.app/wrong\",\n      \"url\": \"https://api.superdocs.app/mcp\",\n      \"headers\": {\n        \"Authorization\": \"Bearer sk_fixture_dupkey_000000\"\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n"
      },
      "expect": {
        "scan": {
          "exit_code": 0,
          "findings": [
            {
              "id": "config.duplicate-keys",
              "severity": "warn",
              "auto_fixable": false
            }
          ],
          "must_not_contain_findings": [
            "config.path-wrong",
            "config.scheme-insecure"
          ]
        },
        "fix": {
          "exit_code": 0,
          "findings": [
            {
              "id": "config.duplicate-keys"
            }
          ],
          "files_unchanged": true,
          "backup_expected": false
        }
      },
      "_why": "The surviving value is correct, so no URL defect fires — but the shadowed one is still reported, because a reader of this file cannot tell which one the client uses. Never auto-fixed: deleting one of a developer's two lines is a guess about intent."
    },
