    {
      "name": "host-rule-policy-gateway",
      "description": "THE HOST RULE. An entry named superdocs pointing at an organisation's policy gateway. --fix must leave it byte-identical: rewriting it to the vendor endpoint would silently disable that gateway's allowlist, content scan, quota and audit.",
      "raw_files": {
        ".mcp.json": "{\n  \"mcpServers\": {\n    \"superdocs\": {\n      \"type\": \"http\",\n      \"url\": \"http://localhost:8080/mcp\",\n      \"headers\": {\n        \"Authorization\": \"Bearer gw_fixture_team_token_00000\"\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n"
      },
      "expect": {
        "scan": {
          "exit_code": 0,
          "findings": [
            {
              "id": "scope.non-canonical-host",
              "severity": "info",
              "auto_fixable": false
            }
          ],
          "must_not_contain_findings": [
            "config.scheme-insecure",
            "config.path-wrong",
            "config.key-shape-unexpected"
          ],
          "no_network_to": [
            "localhost",
            "127.0.0.1"
          ]
        },
        "fix": {
          "exit_code": 0,
          "findings": [
            {
              "id": "scope.non-canonical-host"
            }
          ],
          "files_unchanged": true,
          "backup_expected": false,
          "no_network_to": [
            "localhost",
            "127.0.0.1"
          ]
        }
      },
      "_why": "http:// and a non-standard key prefix would each be a defect on the canonical host. Off it they are none of our business — the host rule short-circuits every URL and credential check, and no probe is sent to the address either."
    },
